            <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>During the walkthrough, we found leakage on the following items:

-Receptacles

-Sawing room window

-Back door

-From the crawl space (water heater room)

During the infiltration test walkthrough, we notice air leakage on the items listed above. Airtightness is very important if you are changing your heating system. We recommend sealing the building before changing the furnace. During the infiltration test, we felt some air leakage coming from the crawl space in the sawing room. Some work are recommended to seal this section.

</airSeal>
                <windows>At the time of the assessment we notice a mix of double and triple-pane windows. We recommend the replacement of the windows by triple-pane and Energy star certified units. </windows>
                <HeatingSystem>Changing the heating system is a big decision and it?????????s not easy to choose. To help you decide we suggest the following points:

-Source of energy 

-Efficiency

-Maintenance

-Cost (To acquire the system and maintenance)

-Your comfort 

Since you have some time ahead, we suggest taking your time to choose the best system that will meet your needs and expectations. 

The suggested upgrade is based on a Condensing Propane Furnace. You may chose a different system. </HeatingSystem>
                <Renewables>For any questions concerning the rebates and the programs about solar energy, please follow the link below to get more information:

https://yukon.ca/en/renewable-energy-rebate#eligible-renewable-systems

PLEASE NOTE: The photovoltaic suggested system, is based on the installation of 6 panels. This is only for suggestion purposes, the system might be composed of more than the suggested system.

</Renewables>
            </RURComments>
        </Options>
